After suffering through playing 3.1 on my 286-10 (my 486 is
busy doing other things...), I decided to play around and see
if I could speed things up.  First thing, since I'm not running
DOS 5 on my 486, I upgraded my 286 to it.  This freed up quite
a bit of conventional memory, but I still didn't notice it much.

I was running my uppoer 300+ memory as a ram-disk, and decided to
try using smartdrv for it.  That seemed to help a whole lot.

Sooo, my suggestion is to get DOS 5 (or a memory manager) and a good
disk cacher.  My machine went from barely usable to slightly slow,
so I am can use this as more than just a terminal. :-)

Kudos to the Nethack Development Team.  GREAT JOB!!

